      "classification": "valid_structural_bridge",
      "reason": "For every support size d≤N the integer alternant quotient has the stated binomial determinant value. Each p-adic pair-count excess over the consecutive support is nonnegative and vanishes exactly at balanced occupancy. The Eisenstein cyclotomic quotient R/(1−ζ)=F_p is correct, so a balanced support gives a nonzero quotient on every list of roots, including repeated roots."
    },
    {
      "id": "confluent-hermite-interpolation",
      "response_lines": [
        80,
        108
      ],
      "classification": "valid_R3_structure",
      "reason": "In the confluent determinant, taking within-block Taylor degrees 0,…,m_i−1 exhausts the total internal Vandermonde degree. Hence cross-block factors and Q contribute only their repeated-node constants, giving the exact normalized-Taylor determinant without missing factorial factors. Its Q factor is a p-unit for balanced A. Therefore all total-d Hermite data are uniquely interpolable and the zero bound counts multiplicities. The factorization of 1−ζ^(p^e u) as p^e factors uses the primitive p^e-root product and each quotient contributes exactly one π, proving the stated cross-block π-order."
    },
    {
      "id": "fixed-bit-reversal-singularity-witness",
      "response_lines": [
        110,
        130
      ],
      "classification": "valid_R3_classification",
      "reason": "Digit reversal sends each length-p^k prefix block to a complete μ_(p^k) coset; the final partial block lies in a new coset. If some occupancy<n_floor, the q full cosets have rank below q p^k and t additions cannot restore rank. Otherwise a count>q+1 gives a class-supported nonzero coefficient vector annihilating all q+1 coset representatives. Thus this single prescribed T_d witnesses every unbalanced support, proving the necessity and all four equivalences."
    },
    {
      "id": "visible-baseline-and-prescribed-multiplicities",
      "response_lines": [
        132,
        142
      ],
      "classification": "valid_baseline_and_extension",
      "reason": "The original three residues remain distinct at every higher p-power level, so the stronger multiplicity bound implies the requested distinct-root bound for every permitted coefficient vector. The binary counterexample on μ_p correctly proves necessity of the original residue condition. Adding one Taylor condition to any total-(d−1) set gives rank d; hence the original conditions have rank d−1, one projective solution and exactly the prescribed total multiplicities with no additional unit-root zero."
    }
